    "An ordinary List may be empty, but this particular conversion always starts with at least one element and keeps it. The returned value is therefore nonempty even though its List<Int> type also permits empty values.",
    "The parameter is NonEmptyList<A>, not Array<A>. To convert an Array to List, use std/array.toList instead. A names the element type and stays the same in the result; conversion does not mutate the input."
